c RUN: %solver --anfread %s --anfwrite /dev/stdout --xl 0 --el 0 --sat 0 --binomred 0 --probe 0 | %OutputCheck %s
c RUN: %solver --anfread %s --solve --allsol --verb 0 | %verify allsol %s
c
c The two XORs share four of their five terms, so adding the first to the
c second leaves x5 + x6, which the replacer turns into an equivalence.
c The nonlinear equation contains the definition x1*x2 + x3 + x7 of x8, so
c it gets rewritten to use x8 instead.
x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5
x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x6
x8 + x1*x2 + x3 + x7
x1*x2 + x3 + x7 + x9*x10 + x11
c CHECK: \[poly-shorten\] shortened 2 eqs
c CHECK-L: x(8) + x(9)*x(10) + x(11)
c CHECK-L: Equivalences
c CHECK-L: x(6) + x(5)
